==Battleground==
*Infinite [[Snache]]s spawn, delay 6.67~13.33 seconds<sup>200f~400f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Croco]]s spawn, delay 6.67~13.33 seconds<sup>200f~400f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Squire Rel]]s spawn, delay 6.67~13.33 seconds<sup>200f~400f</sup>.
*1 [[R.Ost]] spawns after 50 seconds<sup>1,500f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Henry]] spawns as the boss.
**2 [[R.Ost]]s spawn, delay 66.67 seconds<sup>2,000f</sup>.

==Strategy==
With a total of three buffed R.Osts and minimal cash sources, a simple mistake could allow Henry to paralyze your attackers so they could push through your army. Thankfully, the bulk of the threats don't spawn until after base hit. Your goal is to take out the first R.Ost while maximizing your wallet and avoiding the remaining enemies, then lure the R.Osts near your base, and time any others you'd spawn to reduce Henry's impact on your defense. After the two R.Osts are defeated, the stage is effectively won, as Henry and the peons alone are unlikely to even destroy your base.

Alternatively, you could decide to take on the second and third R.Ost at the enemy base, inside Henry's blind spot- so long as you lead up to the base with a wall of meat shields and slower attackers like dragon cats and their variants, as to not hit the base early and have them get caught up in Henry's beam. [[Li'l Tank Cat (Special Cat)|Li'l Eraser Cat]] and [[Lone Cat and Kitten (Rare Cat)|Tourist Cat]], if you have them, are great for helping pinning the R.Osts down.

On higher crown difficulties, this stage becomes significantly less painful, as [[Talents|Talented]] [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]] can use Henry as a stepping stone to reduce the first R.Ost to a pulp and destroy the base before the second is able to spawn. Timing is required, however, as Bahamut may become permanently frozen if sent out at the wrong time.

==='''Recommended Ubers'''===
Generally, any [[:Category:Anti-Traitless Cats|anti-Traitless]] [[:Category:Uber Rare Cats|Uber]]/[[:Category:Legend Rare Cats|Legend Rares]], like most of the [[EPICFEST (Gacha Event)|EPICFEST]] exclusives, or any Ubers that are [[:Category:Cats with Freeze Immunity|immune to freeze]] who also are able to outrange R.Ost should be good in this stage. Below are specified examples of good Ubers to use in this stage.
*[[Snow Miku 2021 (Uber Rare Cat)|Snow Miku 2021]]: An Anti-Traitless Freezer with Long Distance that can even snipe Henry. It's recommended for you to lure the enemies, however, so Henry couldn't effectively disable her.
*[[Relentless Gladios (Uber Rare Cat)|Gladios]]: Another Anti-Traitless crowd controller. It can deal with the R.Osts. Be wary of its sluggish speed and high cost.

